{% doc %}
  Self-hosted fonts (SIL OFL 1.1, see licenses/ in the repo).

  Files are the latin subsets Google Fonts serves to the current site:
  - fraunces-roman.woff2 / fraunces-italic.woff2: variable, opsz 9–144, wght 100–900, SOFT 0–100
  - jost.woff2: variable, wght 100–900 (the theme uses 300/400/500)

  The "Fallback" faces are local system fonts scaled to Fraunces/Jost metrics,
  so the swap from fallback to web font causes (almost) no layout shift.
  Overrides computed with fontTools against macOS Georgia/Arial.

  Rendered in <head> before critical.css. The two primary faces are preloaded
  from layout/theme.liquid.
{% enddoc %}
{% style %}
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Fraunces';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 300 800;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('{{ 'fraunces-roman.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Fraunces';
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 300 800;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('{{ 'fraunces-italic.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Jost';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 300 500;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url('{{ 'jost.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Fraunces Fallback';
    font-style: normal;
    src: local('Georgia');
    size-adjust: 106.05%;
    ascent-override: 92.22%;
    descent-override: 24.05%;
    line-gap-override: 0%;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Fraunces Fallback';
    font-style: italic;
    src: local('Georgia Italic'), local('Georgia-Italic');
    size-adjust: 98.86%;
    ascent-override: 98.93%;
    descent-override: 25.79%;
    line-gap-override: 0%;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Jost Fallback';
    font-style: normal;
    src: local('Arial'), local('ArialMT');
    size-adjust: 92.71%;
    ascent-override: 115.41%;
    descent-override: 40.45%;
    line-gap-override: 0%;
  }
{% endstyle %}
